{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And you came near to me, all of you.</b> Even though you had appointed leaders over you for public needs, you all came yourselves." "<b>Let us send men.</b> We ourselves will choose the men and send them. Therefore the El, exalted be He, did not agree, and said to Moses: שְׁלַח לְךָ (Numbers 13:2) — that he himself should choose the men, not they, lest they choose ordinary men who would make things worse. And so Moses chose כֻּלָּם אֲנָשִׁים (Numbers 13:3), among them Joshua and Caleb. And even the wicked among them, though they sinned in saying it was impossible to conquer, did not have the audacity to say the land was bad, but reported its praise — so that afterward they repented, as it says: וַתַּעֲנוּ וַתֹּאמְרוּ אֵלַי חָטָאנוּ לַה׳ (Deuteronomy 1:41), וַתָּשֻׁבוּ וַתִּבְכּוּ לִפְנֵי ה׳ (Deuteronomy 1:45)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:08.842601225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}